---
import BaseLayoutV2 from '../layouts/BaseLayoutV2.astro';
import EmailCaptureForm from '../components/EmailCaptureForm.tsx';
---
<BaseLayoutV2
  title="GreenSquare | The brief that survives senior scrutiny"
  description="GreenSquare turns Claude or GPT into a disciplined decision advisor. It interrogates before it answers, then gives you an evidence-tagged recommendation you can defend."
  current="home"
>
  <!-- HERO — light, clean, oversized-but-balanced -->
  <section class="v-section v-off hero">
    <div class="v-container">
      <div class="v-split is-top">
        <div class="v-reveal">
          <h1 class="v-display">The brief that survives senior scrutiny.</h1>
          <p class="v-lead" style="margin-top: var(--v-6);">
            Think through any decision and come out with something you would stand behind. GreenSquare turns a
            generic AI into a disciplined thinking partner: it questions you before it answers, frames the real
            call, generates genuine options, and hands you an evidence-tagged recommendation, in markdown, with
            the same interrogation method and five-part output structure across Claude, ChatGPT and Gemini.
          </p>
          <div class="hero-actions">
            <a class="v-btn v-btn--green" href="#frame">Get the free Decision Frame</a>
            <a class="v-btn v-btn--grey" href="/benchmark/">See the benchmark</a>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="v-reveal d1">
          <div class="v-readout">
            <div class="v-readout__bar"><span class="v-readout__dot"></span> DECISION_BRIEF.md</div>
            <div class="v-readout__body">
              <ul class="v-spec__list">
                <li><span class="n">/01</span> The decision, and why now</li>
                <li><span class="n">/02</span> The options, compared</li>
                <li><span class="n">/03</span> The recommendation</li>
                <li><span class="n">/04</span> Next steps</li>
                <li><span class="n">/05</span> What would change this call</li>
              </ul>
              <div class="spec-tags">
                <span class="v-tag">given</span><span class="v-tag">derived</span><span class="v-tag">inferred</span><span class="v-tag">unknown</span>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="v-readout__foot">MARKDOWN OUTPUT <span class="v-cursor" aria-hidden="true"></span></div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- PULL-QUOTE — the one serif editorial beat -->
  <section class="v-section v-fill">
    <div class="v-container">
      <p class="v-quote v-reveal">Most AI answers the question you typed. GreenSquare asks what a good adviser would ask first.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- THREE PILLARS — indexed capability list -->
  <section class="v-section">
    <div class="v-container">
      <h2 class="v-h2" style="max-width: 24ch;">Three things a generic answer skips.</h2>
      <div class="v-caplist">
        <div class="v-caprow v-reveal">
          <span class="v-index">/01</span>
          <h3>It interrogates before it answers</h3>
          <p class="v-small v-cap-body">
            It asks what a good adviser would ask first, tests the framing once, plays the situation back to
            you, and catches where your own answers contradict each other, before it produces anything.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="v-caprow v-reveal d1">
          <span class="v-index">/02</span>
          <h3>It shows its evidence</h3>
          <p class="v-small v-cap-body">
            Every claim the call rests on is tagged given, derived, inferred or unknown, and the recommendation names
            the single assumption it stands on.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="v-caprow v-reveal d2">
          <span class="v-index">/03</span>
          <h3>It holds a consulting standard, on any model</h3>
          <p class="v-small v-cap-body">
            The discipline is encoded in the file, so the output holds the same structure across Claude, ChatGPT
            and Gemini, and scales effort to the stakes rather than over-engineering a small call.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- EVIDENCE — big green block, operational readout -->
  <section class="v-section v-green">
    <div class="v-container v-split is-reverse">
      <div class="v-reveal">
        <h2 class="v-h2">Same model, same question. Different brief.</h2>
        <p class="v-lead" style="margin-top: var(--v-5);">
          Given only the question a real person would paste, a naked baseline reframes the problem, but sizes the
          risk at roughly 8% of revenue and never sees the mechanism that actually kills the deal. Loaded with
          the Decision, the same model interrogates the facts out, reaches close to 40% of the division, and
          lands a brief you could defend.
        </p>
        <a class="v-link" href="/benchmark/" style="display:inline-block; margin-top: var(--v-6);">Read the full comparison</a>
      </div>
      <div class="v-reveal d1">
        <div class="v-readout">
          <div class="v-readout__bar"><span class="v-readout__dot"></span> BENCHMARK / DEFENSIBLE_BRIEF</div>
          <div class="v-readout__body">
            <div class="v-run">
              <div class="v-run__head"><span class="v-run__name">NAKED BASELINE</span><span class="v-run__val">risk 8% / structure 0/3</span></div>
              <div class="v-meter"><div class="v-meter__fill is-muted" style="--w: 7%;"></div></div>
            </div>
            <div class="v-run">
              <div class="v-run__head"><span class="v-run__name">INFORMED BASELINE</span><span class="v-run__val">structure 0/3</span></div>
              <div class="v-meter"><div class="v-meter__fill is-muted" style="--w: 7%;"></div></div>
            </div>
            <div class="v-run">
              <div class="v-run__head"><span class="v-run__name">THE DECISION</span><span class="v-run__val"><b>risk 40% / structure 3/3</b></span></div>
              <div class="v-meter"><div class="v-meter__fill" style="--w: 100%;"></div></div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="v-readout__foot">DESIGN-PHASE PILOT / N=3 / CASE A / CLAUDE OPUS 4.8</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- FREE FRAME — one unified, balanced card -->
  <section class="v-section v-fill" id="frame">
    <div class="v-container">
      <div class="v-card frame-card v-reveal">
        <div class="frame-card__grid">
          <div>
            <h2 class="v-h2">Frame the decision before you evaluate anything.</h2>
            <p class="v-measure" style="margin-top: var(--v-5); color: var(--v-ink-soft);">
              The Decision Frame is a free one-page tool that interrogates your decision before you weigh options:
              the real question, the false binary, the load-bearing assumption, and what you actually know. Then it
              hands you to the Decision to decide.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="frame-card__form">
            <EmailCaptureForm client:visible buttonLabel="Send me the free Decision Frame" />
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- SPLIT CTA — differentiated: capture (grey) + evidence (green) -->
  <section class="v-splitcta" aria-label="Get started">
    <div class="v-splitcta__panel v-splitcta__panel--fill v-reveal">
      <div>
        <h2 class="v-h2" style="font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 2.6vw, 2rem);">Start with the free frame.</h2>
        <p class="v-small" style="margin-top: var(--v-4); max-width: 42ch;">The one-page Decision Frame, free. Interrogate the decision before you weigh a single option.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="width: 100%; max-width: 440px;">
        <EmailCaptureForm client:visible buttonLabel="Send me the free frame" />
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="v-splitcta__panel v-splitcta__panel--green v-reveal d1">
      <div>
        <h2 class="v-h2">The proof, pre-registered.</h2>
        <p class="v-lead" style="margin-top: var(--v-4);">Fifty-four runs, two frontier models, a sealed answer key. Only the loaded product produced a defensible brief, every run.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="v-splitcta__action">
        <a class="v-btn v-btn--on-green v-splitcta__btn" href="/benchmark/">See the benchmark</a>
        <p class="v-splitcta__note">No email needed. Read the full method.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayoutV2>

<style>
  .hero { padding-top: clamp(3rem, 6vh, 5rem); }
  .hero-actions { display: flex; gap: var(--v-4); align-items: center; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-top: var(--v-8); }
  .spec-tags { display: flex; gap: var(--v-2); flex-wrap: wrap; margin-top: var(--v-2); }
  .frame-card { padding: clamp(1.75rem, 4vw, var(--v-10)); }
  .frame-card__grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1.1fr 0.9fr; gap: clamp(var(--v-6), 4vw, var(--v-10)); align-items: center; }
  @media (max-width: 760px) { .frame-card__grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: var(--v-8); } }
</style>
